{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1360113-using-higher-level-psi-powers","id":1360113,"title":"Using higher level psi powers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-10T06:15:20-08:00","id":1360113,"title":"Using higher level psi powers","content":"I\u2019m aware that for a higher difficulty and psi cost somebody with translocation at 2 dots could attempt a translocation 4 or 5 power. What if that character has zero dots in transportal? Can they even attempt a mode in their primary aptitude that they possess zero dots in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T09:21:39-08:00","id":1360139,"title":"","content":"Not with my books right now, but I probably wouldn't allow that. I'd rule that you need at least one dot in a mode before you can stretch to reach the higher modes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T09:44:27-08:00","id":1360144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werlynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1360113-using-higher-level-psi-powers#post1360113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m aware that for a higher difficulty and psi cost somebody with translocation at 2 dots could attempt a translocation 4 or 5 power. What if that character has zero dots in transportal? Can they even attempt a mode in their primary aptitude that they possess zero dots in?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can't find a citation for it,but I believe you have to have at least 1 dot in the mode to attempt the power. Even checked the Character Creation chapter thinking it would be snuck in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T10:22:15-08:00","id":1360157,"title":"","content":"It doesn't say, but I've been running it that way. I might change that, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T12:32:19-08:00","id":1360186,"title":"","content":"If you don\u2019t have any dots you can\u2019t use the Mode at all. You need at least one dot to access the Mode\u2019s powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T13:46:47-08:00","id":1360195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1360113-using-higher-level-psi-powers?p=1360186#post1360186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don\u2019t have any dots you can\u2019t use the Mode at all. You need at least one dot to access the Mode\u2019s powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that mean that Psiads can do the same thing (A Psiad with 3 Dots in a Mode can access Dots from 4 and 5 Dots)? Or do they still have a hard limit?<br /> <br /> For my part, I'll probably apply a House Rule that Psions can't access more than 2 levels above their current Dots in a Mode (so they'd need 3 dots to try to get a five dot power).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T14:07:50-08:00","id":1360198,"title":"","content":"Psiads can reach higher dot powers as long as they don\u2019t go over their hard cap. A Psi 3 psiad couldn\u2019t push above a 3 dot power in their primary Aptitudes or a 2 dot power in their secondary, while a Psi 5 psiad couldn\u2019t push beyond 3 dot powers in primary or secondary. (Strong Mode could add one to this in that Mode, of course.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T18:47:44-08:00","id":1360256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1360113-using-higher-level-psi-powers?p=1360198#post1360198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Psiads can reach higher dot powers as long as they don\u2019t go over their hard cap. A Psi 3 psiad couldn\u2019t push above a 3 dot power in their primary Aptitudes or a 2 dot power in their secondary, while a Psi 5 psiad couldn\u2019t push beyond 3 dot powers in primary or secondary. (Strong Mode could add one to this in that Mode, of course.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is there a thread to suggest erratta to the print books? From my reading of Aexpansion, that's not entirely clear, so you might want to add a word or two the print edition making it clear that it's a hard cap, because a fair number of people who have read it think that is a way for an psiad to access level 4-5 powers. <br /> <br /> So just to clarifiy-- a psiad can <i>never</i> have more than 5 dots in a primary mode (with strong mode) or four dots in a secondary mode (again with strong mode).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T19:31:28-08:00","id":1360270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1360113-using-higher-level-psi-powers?p=1360186#post1360186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don\u2019t have any dots you can\u2019t use the Mode at all. You need at least one dot to access the Mode\u2019s powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>thank you <br /> That\u2019s what I thought","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T19:32:25-08:00","id":1360271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, a psiad can't attempt to manifest powers beyond their Mode maximum limitations, as determined by their Psi trait. </div> </div> </div>Page 88. I disagree that it\u2019s not clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T19:57:49-08:00","id":1360276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1360113-using-higher-level-psi-powers?p=1360256#post1360256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Is there a thread to suggest erratta to the print books? From my reading of Aexpansion, that's not entirely clear, so you might want to add a word or two the print edition making it clear that it's a hard cap, because a fair number of people who have read it think that is a way for an psiad to access level 4-5 powers.<br /> <br /> So just to clarifiy-- a psiad can <i>never</i> have more than 5 dots in a primary mode (with strong mode) or four dots in a secondary mode (again with strong mode).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's right. And even with Strong Mode they can't get past four dots in one Primary mode until they reach Psi 6 and Tier III. Psiads are broad, while Psions are deep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}